WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.235
-♪ Look into the box ♪

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.804
♪ The suggestion box ♪

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:09.208
-This first one here
is from Mia Cicero.

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.143
"Hey, Jimmy,
I hear if you dim the lights

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:13.045
and say 'Rockefeller'
three times,

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:15.515
the ghost of Rockefeller Center
will appear.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.982
Can you try this?"

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:20.119
I don't think that's true,
but, um, I can try.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.856
Can we --
Can we dim the lights?

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.795
Rockefeller, Rockefeller,
Rockefeller.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.665
[ Thunder crashes ]

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.836
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:40.840
I'm the ghost
of Rockefeller Center.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.174
-Oh, my God.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:45.011
W-What are you doing here?
W-What do you want?

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.914
-I have haunted
these halls for years,

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.684
but since you ask, real quick,
what is your Wi-Fi password?

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:54.987
[ Laughter ]
-I'm sorry. What?

00:00:54.987 --> 00:00:57.490
-Well, it can get pretty boring
roaming the halls,

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.291
and I'm spending
a fortune on data

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.494
keeping up with
my Insta stories.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.129
-Um, totally.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:07.700
It's -- it's...
NBC 2019, 14 zeros...

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.470
lowercase "n," uppercase "Y."

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:12.739
-So lowercase "n"?

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.641
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:16.742
-Yes.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:18.745
-14 zeros, yes?

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.047
-Yeah, come on. Yeah.
-Ah, I'm connected!

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:25.051
Finally! After 60 years,
I have Internet!

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.586
I'm going to go binge
"Nailed It!" on Netflix.

00:01:27.586 --> 00:01:30.056
Piece out.
-All right, bye, ghost.

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.991
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:37.663
Glad I could help him out.

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.598
Next on here is from
Diana Brennan.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:40.967
"Hey, Jimmy, I'm really excited

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.002
for that new 'Breaking Bad'
movie to come out

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.403
on Netflix this weekend.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.472
I love 'Breaking Bad'
theme song,

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.574
but I noticed
it doesn't have any lyrics.

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.543
Could you do anything
about that?"

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.311
Absolutely.

00:01:52.311 --> 00:01:54.447
I can't wait for it, either.
It looks great.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:57.316
So in honor of "El Camino:
A Breaking Bad Movie,"

00:01:57.316 --> 00:02:00.386
please welcome country-music
superstar Trace Adkins

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:03.156
joined by
the "Breaking Bad" choir.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.191
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:12.866
♪♪

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:15.601
-♪ Was a high school teacher
till he got real sick ♪

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.738
-♪ Now he's breaking bad,
now he's breaking bad ♪

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:22.174
-♪ Aaron Paul was his friend
who called everybody bitch ♪

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:24.777
-♪ He was breaking bad,
also breaking bad ♪

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.447
-♪ Started cooking up drugs,
but they came out blue ♪

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:31.217
-♪ He was breaking bad,
making drugs is bad ♪

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:34.487
-♪ Bought a pork pie hat,
threw a pizza on the roof ♪

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:37.589
-♪ 'Cause he's breaking bad,
really breaking bad ♪

00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:40.560
-♪ Was a big shootout,
and he wound up dead ♪

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.662
-♪ You just spoiled it, dude,
spoiling stuff is bad ♪

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:47.066
-♪ If you haven't seen the show,
never mind what I said ♪

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:49.502
-♪ Check out "Breaking Bad,"
Netflix, "Breaking Bad" ♪

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:55.675
-♪ Breaking Bad ♪

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:59.445
♪ Breaking ♪

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:02.548
♪ Bad ♪

00:03:02.548 --> 00:03:04.483
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:08.421
-Trace Adkins, everyone!
Trace Adkins!

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.723
♪♪

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:14.059
You can see Trace on the
"Ultimate Cowboy Showdown"

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:17.596
on INSP Network
beginning October 14th.

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.498
Trace Adkins.
How cool is that?

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:21.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:25.071
♪ Breaking Bad ♪

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:27.940
This next one is from
Marco Trimboli.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:31.076
Marco, you out there?
Perfect.

00:03:31.076 --> 00:03:32.578
Marco says, "Hey, Jimmy.

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:34.046
Halloween's right
around the corner.

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.716
Can you tell us what the hottest
costumes are this season?"

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:38.517
Well, sure.

00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:40.320
I do have my finger
on the pulse,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.454
and I can easily tell you
what they are,

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:45.224
but I'd rather just show you,
so, ladies and gentlemen,

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:48.060
here are this year's
hottest Halloween costumes.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:50.096
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.998
The first costume is
going to be huge this year.

00:03:52.998 --> 00:03:54.867
It's the Notebook Boy.

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.637
All you need is a friend,
two Moleskine notebooks,

00:03:58.637 --> 00:04:00.340
and a preppy outfit.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:01.941
You and your friend
will be the only thing

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.710
anyone's talking about
at your Halloween party.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.812
The Notebook Boy.

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:11.016
Our next costume
is Heinrich Von Chowder.

00:04:11.016 --> 00:04:13.986
It's a fun twist on your
classic Oktoberfest outfit

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:18.057
where you get to walk around
with giant steins

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:20.860
filled with piping-hot
creamy soup.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.729
Yeah.

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:26.499
Our next costume --

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.868
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.303
Our next costume is a fun one.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:31.637
It's the GIF of your friend

00:04:31.637 --> 00:04:34.072
walking into their
surprise party.

00:04:34.072 --> 00:04:36.775
For this costume, all you
have to do is get a white box

00:04:36.775 --> 00:04:39.812
and then repeat the same motion
for hours and hours

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:42.648
until you can no longer
feel your face.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:45.351
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.353
Our next costume
is based on something

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:49.221
I think we've all
had to deal with.

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:51.490
It's the guy from high school
who claims he didn't get

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:54.627
butt implants
but definitely did.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.662
We all have that friend.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:05:00.133
He seems pretty normal,
but then he got butt implants.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.735
But acts like he totally didn't.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:05.337
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:09.809
And here's our final costume.
It is the Longest Horse.

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:13.345
Two-person horse costumes
are so last year.

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:16.582
2019 is the year of the horse.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.083
The long horse.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:22.321
Giddy-up into the number-one
Halloween costume this fall.

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:25.691
The best part is,
it's super-easy to navigate.

00:05:25.691 --> 00:05:27.994
You'll barely knock over
any furniture

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.728
at your next Halloween
get-together,

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:32.397
and matching shoes and tights
are sold separately.

00:05:32.397 --> 00:05:35.334
It's going to be
a great Halloween.

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:37.436
Enjoy those costume, everybody.
There you go.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.272
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:46.211
Let's try one more suggestion
from the old sugg box here.

00:05:46.211 --> 00:05:50.115
This one is from Dave Sinclair.

00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:52.385
He said, "Hey, Jimmy.
I know people at the club

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.820
usually dance
to fast, upbeat music.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:56.088
But recently at work,

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.057
I heard the printer
printing a bunch of copies,

00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.359
and the printer
was making a fun beat.

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:02.795
Can you have people dance
to a printer's beat?"

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:04.730
I think we can make that happen.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.066
There's a local musician
who plays using a printer.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:10.202
So give it up for
DJ Eight-and-A-Half-By-Eleven.

00:06:10.202 --> 00:06:11.937
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:11.937 --> 00:06:14.507
[ Printer whirring
rhythmically ]

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:22.381
[ EDM music joins ]

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:29.088
♪♪

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.590
-That's all the time we have
for Audience Suggestion Box.

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.560
Stick around. We'll be right
back with Clive Owen, everybody.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.832
♪♪

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:45.071
♪♪

